      "writtenOn": "2017-08-19T12:13:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe what I really want is to get some idea of what is going to happen from the task name.\n\nIn CORD codebase frequently \"Ensure ...\" tasks names are like mystery meat - without reading the task, you don\u0027t know what might happen.\n\n\"Ensure SSH Keypair\" falls into that category - it could be the current behavior, or a copy of the keys to the remote machine, or just an assertion that the file exists and nothing new might be created.\n\n\"Ensure SSH keypair is created for ansible login user\" would meet this goal but still uses \"Ensure\".",
      "parentUuid": "3a3291f1_cff48189",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 17,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 17,
        "endChar": 14
